+
+## Specification admission and immutable development handoff
+
+CLI and daemon readers open one specification descriptor with O_NONBLOCK,
+require a regular file by fstat, and read at most 1 MiB plus one rejection byte.
+Metadata and byte limits are both checked; the reader also rejects a file whose
+ownership, mode, size or modification metadata changes while held. Ordinary
+CLI symlinks remain supported. This does not promise a deadline for stalled
+remote filesystems or freeze the images named by the specification.
+
+Non-root daemon peers retain the root-owned, non-group/other-writable file
+policy inside the configured specification directory. The daemon walks held
+directory descriptors without following replacement components and checks the
+same file descriptor it reads. A canonical parent-directory alias is accepted;
+a symlink specification leaf is refused. Peer-UID authorization and CellSpec
+validation still precede activation.
+
+The development parent serializes the admitted CellSpec into a CLOEXEC memfd
+and installs F_SEAL_WRITE, F_SEAL_GROW, F_SEAL_SHRINK and F_SEAL_SEAL before host
+setup. The private entry accepts --sealed-spec with a version-1 JSON binding:
+fd number, device, inode, exact byte length and SHA-256. Only the spawned child's
+pre-exec descriptor table becomes inheritable; the multithreaded daemon keeps
+CLOEXEC set. This hook appends to the existing parent-death/ownership hooks.
+
+A real root entry verifies the inherited descriptor, owner, mode, all seals,
+length and digest, uses bounded pread independent of the inherited file offset,
+and closes the original inherited slot after successful consumption. Its
+temporary duplicate is CLOEXEC and closes before Android construction. The
+binding grants no authority to a non-root process. An explicit root caller may
+still use the private --spec pathname form, while daemon and development-run
+always use the sealed protocol. A launcher that closes or substitutes the
+descriptor fails closed.
+
+These input and handoff guarantees do not implement production UID/GID mapping,
+seccomp, resource isolation or Android/application runtime qualification.
 
